3: Chapter 3: Trainer of Spikemuth\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The dawn in the Sunset Forest was silent, as hardly any bird Pok\u233?mon could be seen here.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The creaking sound of stepping on wooden stairs at this moment seemed particularly harsh. The sound-sensitive Grookey immediately opened its eyes, realizing there was a stranger around. It hastily nudged Summer, who was still asleep.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Huh? What's wrong, Grookey?" Summer sat up, rubbing his eyes. He hadn't fully adjusted to waking up early yet.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With a sudden click, the wooden door was pushed open. Grookey felt a bit scared at first, but remembering Summer's kindness, it mustered up the courage and took the wooden stick off its head, assuming a defensive posture.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ah!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ah!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The girl who pushed open the wooden door and Summer, who was sitting on the bed, looked at each other, and the scene became awkward for a moment.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The girl had an expressionless face, with a hint of confusion in her eyes. She wore a cute pink dress, paired with a punk-style black jacket, giving her a unique charm that was hard to describe.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Summer suddenly became more awake. He recognized the girl in front of him, a trainer from Spikemuth, Marnie, also a popular idol in Spikemuth, with her own fan club called Team Yell.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Out of politeness, Marnie cleared her throat and asked, "Who are you, and why are you sleeping here? Are you a passing trainer?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
To prove his legitimacy, Summer reluctantly replied, "I'm Summer Leaf, a new forest ranger in Sunset Forest."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With that, he got up, picked up his jacket from the chair, and took off his badge.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"If you don't believe me, I have my badge here to prove my identity."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Forest ranger, huh? It must be tough being a forest ranger in such a remote forest."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But wait, am I the one being comforted? But since she acknowledges my identity, there shouldn't be any misunderstanding.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"My name is Marnie, a trainer from Spikemuth. Sorry for disturbing you, Mr. Forest Ranger."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Marnie bowed apologetically. At that moment, Morpeko poked its head out of her backpack, happily munching on tree fruits, one after another.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Overall, it's because of this little one." Marnie patted Morpeko's head. "I came to this forest to look for tree fruits and then found this cabin, so I used it as my secret base."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Tree fruits, huh? Morpeko can get aggressive when hungry," Summer said, looking at Morpeko. He was quite knowledgeable about all Pok\u233?mon living in the forest now.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That's right, but that's also part of its charm," Marnie said with a fond look in her eyes and a rare smile on her lips.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"In that case, you must be the owner of those books," Summer suddenly said.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Pok\u233?dex for Dark-type Pok\u233?mon, how to communicate with people, the essential knowledge for trainers, all of it matches up with Marnie's interests. Summer felt relieved; thankfully, it seemed there was no ghostly activity.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Marnie's cheeks blushed instantly. She quickly ran to the bookshelf, put three books into her backpack, and as she noticed Summer witnessing her rare moment, Morpeko flashed a smile and waved its little hand.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Did you see?" Marnie asked softly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I flipped through them a bit. After all, I needed to check what was inside the cabin."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ah, it's so embarrassing!" Marnie blushed even more, feeling exposed about her hobby. She wished she could disappear into the ground.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No, Marnie, you're not that crybaby anymore. She clenched her fists, encouraging herself. So what if he saw it? Just admit it boldly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Marnie took a deep breath, calmed herself, and then turned around to face Summer seriously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes, I like Dark-type Pok\u233?mon and battling! I like it very much! So much that I can't even handle it!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ignoring the part about communication with people? Well, it's better to give her an out now.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh, that's a nice hobby," Summer responded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Facing Summer's reply, Marnie pursed her lips, still blushing slightly. Her black eyes stared at the floor, silent for a while, then muttered softly:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"As for the content of the last book, please keep it a secret, Mr. Summer."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Sure, I'll keep it a secret," Summer replied calmly, thinking that refusing might lead to being hunted down by Team Yell.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With a positive response, Marnie gradually regained her usual expression. Still feeling a bit embarrassed about her outburst, she suddenly asked:\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Mr. Summer, what do forest rangers do?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Well, simply put, we protect the forest and the Pok\u233?mon in it."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Summer, neatly dressed, extended his arm, and Grookey swiftly jumped onto his shoulder. Then, he sat down on the edge of the bed and began to explain to Marnie.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
