12: Chapter 12: Pok\u233?mon Hunter Appears in Southeast Sunset Forest\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A message flashed: [A Pok\u233?mon Hunter has appeared in the southeast of Sunset Forest.]\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Summer jolted awake from his sleep. Beside him, Grookey rubbed its eyes, looking at Summer in confusion.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Pok\u233?mon hunter," Summer murmured.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Pok\u233?mon hunters are dangerous individuals engaged in illegal activities. They capture rare Pok\u233?mon to sell on the black market for high profits and are targets of the League's strict crackdown.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As a ranger of Sunset Forest, Summer was responsible for ensuring the Pok\u233?mon in the forest were not harmed by these hunters.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He quickly got dressed and told Grookey, "Someone is threatening the Pok\u233?mon in the forest. Grookey, we need to move quickly."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Grookey immediately woke up at Summer's words, giving him a determined look before jumping onto Summer's shoulder.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Heh, this operation was a success," chuckled a tall, thin man in a black coat, looking at the six Morpeko in the cage. He's Blank, a novice Pok\u233?mon hunter.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Beside Blank, a Thievul let out a sly cry, matching its owner's demeanor.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But it's strange. These Morpeko neither eat berries nor change forms. The berries I prepared were wasted."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The thin man threw down the bag in his hand. He had heard rumors of many Morpeko in this forest, prompting his poaching expedition.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hmph, but this will fetch a good price." He rubbed his hands, eyes gleaming with greed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Morpeko wasn't rare in Galar, but in other regions, it was different\u8212?they were scarcely found.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Blank planned to smuggle them to the Kanto region and sell them on the black market. Residents there were known for their love of electric rodents. They wouldn't miss a region-exclusive Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"With this money, I'll turn my life around. Once I'm rich, I'll make those guys lick my boots."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The thin man fantasized about spending lavishly and attracting envious glances. Suddenly, he felt something tugging at his pant leg. Looking down, he saw Thievul.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What's wrong? Can't you see I'm happy?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Blank followed Thievul's gaze to see a Morpeko peeking from behind a tree, staring at him with its round eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Another one? Great, the more the better."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He picked up his net and sneaked towards the Morpeko, seeing it as a piece of shining gold.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Suddenly, two sharp leaves flew out from the dark forest, slicing through Blank's net.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What the\u8212?!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Blank's face twisted in fear. He swung his stick and shouted into the forest, but only his echo answered.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Is it the forest's Pok\u233?mon? Hey, Thievul, come here."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He backed towards Thievul, sweat dripping from his forehead.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thievul leapt to Blank's side, looking ahead with its brown eyes and let out a piercing howl. Dark energy spread towards the forest.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Stop hiding and face me!" Blank shouted to bolster his courage. He had chosen to come at night to avoid detection.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Two sharp leaves flew from behind him. Thievul leapt up, deflecting one leaf with its bushy tail, but a chunk of the tail was cut off.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"See? Not so strong. Thievul, don't worry about me, just take out the hiding one. Your nose is sharp."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Blank felt inexplicably confident. Thievul, however, looked exasperated. Its master wasn't very bright, but given the constant ambush, their opponent's raw power must be lacking.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Deciding to attack, Thievul's cunning nature meant it only acted with certainty of victory.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It darted towards the source of the Razor Leaf, baring its sharp teeth.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Now, Branch Poke!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Summer's shout made Thievul hesitate. Branch Poke? Weak. Watch me deal with you.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thievul, full of confidence, saw Grookey charge from the darkness, its stick glowing green. Thievul opened its mouth wide, ready to tear the small monkey apart.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Roar!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
I can't breathe. It hurts. What's happening? Such power!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thievul's eyes widened as it glimpsed the ground. A stick was pressed against its throat. Grookey pulled it out, giving Thievul a moment to gasp.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This opponent is unbeatable. I need to escape, now!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Grookey grabbed Thievul's face, flipping onto its head. Thievul couldn't track Grookey's movements. The glowing stick struck Thievul's head, making it dizzy and crashing its jaw into the ground.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Acrobatics."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Grookey, glowing green, moved like a green blur, striking Thievul multiple times in a flash. Thievul received four punches, three kicks, and a final stick strike to its side.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thievul collapsed, losing the battle. Blank's smile froze. He couldn't believe his Thievul was defeated instantly by a beginner Pok\u233?mon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Summer emerged from the forest, glancing at the caged Morpeko before turning to Blank, who stood in shock.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Optimizing the Custap Berries had caused Morpeko not to change to Hangry Mode, making them non-aggressive and easy to capture.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Who are you?" Blank demanded, snapping out of it. How could someone be here at this hour?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'm the ranger of this forest," Summer replied coldly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Blank's face turned ashen. Being caught poaching by a ranger was as bad as being caught by the police. Poaching was one of the most severe crimes against the League.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I've never done this before. Please, let me go. These annoying Pok\u233?mon must be a pain for you too, right?" Blank pleaded, hoping Summer's kind face would spare him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Where's the key?" Summer asked, walking towards Blank.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Here, here." Blank awkwardly smiled, tossing the key. He watched Summer bend down to pick it up and bolted.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As long as I escape, they can't convict me. I'll be free...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the dark, Corvisquire swooped down, startling Blank, who fell to the ground.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's over."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hah, hah, it's society's fault I'm like this. If I had a proper job like you...!" Blank tried to argue.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Summer took out a rope, tightly binding Blank. His cold eyes showed no mercy under the moonlight.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Eek!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Blank fainted, foaming at the mouth. In his last moment of consciousness, he heard Summer's merciless words.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Save that nonsense for the police."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
(End of Chapter)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} 
