"Plus, the berry shops have a steady supply from berry farms. If the shop gains popularity and we can't meet demand, what then? Are you, a forest ranger, going to compete with the Pok\u233?mon for food?" Gideon questioned.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He knew that running a business wasn't easy. Despite his confidence in his curry, few would travel to this declining town just for a plate of curry.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Grandpa Gideon, the attraction of Sunset Forest berries is greater than curry."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Gideon choked on his tea, coughing violently and widening his eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Cough, cough, you rascal, if I didn't know you meant well for Spikemuth, I'd knock you out."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You've tasted the Sunset Forest berries yourself. How are they?" Summer asked directly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Well," Gideon hesitated, then reluctantly admitted, "they're delicious, that's true."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But," he started to argue.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"First, I don't plan to open a shop in Spikemuth. I intend to sell to other berry shops, just like before."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Seeing Summer's earnest eyes, Gideon softened. Summer was a good kid trying to revive Spikemuth. He should hear him out before offering advice.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Firstly, we can keep the price low but must brand them as from Spikemuth. Given the sales at Hammerlocke, the shop owners should agree."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The key is reputation. We need people to remember Spikemuth."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"As for supply, I've considered it. The yield of Sunset Forest berries will only increase in the future."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What if the shop owners don't agree?" Gideon asked, joining the discussion.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"As long as the quality is good and the price is low, someone will agree. Our cost is almost zero."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Are you really a ranger?" Gideon asked helplessly. "And once people are drawn in?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"We show them Spikemuth's charm, which you know better than I do."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Of course." Gideon finished his tea in one gulp, setting the cup down with a clink. "This is a gradual process. You still have your ranger duties, so leave the promotion to me. I still have some connections."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
He smiled, "That's why you came to me, right?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Exactly."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I understand. But Summer, why are you so determined to revive Spikemuth?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Maybe it's the charm of Spikemuth." Summer's words were sincere.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hearing this, Gideon stood up and headed to the kitchen, leaving a final word.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Sit tight. I'll treat you to a meal."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After that day, high-quality berries branded with Spikemuth's name began appearing in berry shops across Galar, quickly becoming popular among trainers. People started to grow curious about Spikemuth, the origin of these berries.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
At Macro Cosmos HQ, President Rose toyed with a plump, juicy Sitrus Berry.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Look at this, Oleana. Such a beautiful berry. I hear it's quite delicious too."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes, President Rose. According to our research, this berry's quality is 60% higher than average Sitrus Berries." Oleana reported from her notes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Impressive," Rose admired.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Shall we send our team to\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
