Meanwhile, in Hulbury, a port city in eastern Galar, Marnie had just finished her Grass-type Gym Challenge and arrived in town.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Summer said to visit the berry shop here. Morpeko, what surprise do you think he has in store?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Morpeko~" Morpeko mumbled, mouth full of berries.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Right, with you around, I'd go to the berry shop even if Summer hadn't mentioned it."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Marnie felt her success in the Gym Challenge was thanks to Summer's advice, so she thanked him on Chuchu, receiving a response.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Nothing special here," Marnie said, scanning the berry shop, then spotted something interesting. "What's this?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
An empty basket had a wooden nameplate reading: Berries from Spikemuth.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"So this is your surprise, Summer."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Marnie instantly understood Summer's intent. He was using the Sunset Forest berries to promote Spikemuth, his clever idea.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Everyone's working hard, so I must work even harder."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Marnie whispered encouragement to herself. Wait and see, Summer, the fame I bring to Spikemuth will surpass yours. I won't lose this competition!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
(End of Chapter)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} 
