24: Chapter 24: Temporal Distortion - Misty Grassland\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After reaching an agreement with Grandpa Gideon on the plan for promoting berries, Summer's life as a forest ranger returned to tranquility.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Every day, he patrolled Sunset Forest, checking trees and grass, occasionally assisting Pok\u233?mon training in the forest, and helping everyone with berry picking.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Marnie's Gym Challenge journey also went smoothly. With her ace Morpeko, she easily conquered the Hulbury Stadium. Due to her outstanding performance, her fan base gradually grew.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The promotion of berries and Marnie's Gym Challenge complemented each other. As Grandpa Gideon said, people were now deliberately visiting Spikemuth.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The despondent townsfolk saw hope. Now Spikemuth was undergoing a vigorous transformation, aiming to leave a good impression on tourists and not disappoint Summer, Marnie, and everyone's efforts.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Here, Phantump, this wooden badge belongs to you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
In the cabin in the woods, Summer hung the wooden badge with the position engraved on it on a branch above Phantump's head. It was the third Phantump born in Sunset Forest.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Then, Phantump's two predecessors floated over and touched its head with their branches. This was the unique way Phantump communicated, conveying joy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Please continue to protect the forest. Good luck."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
