"Really? I think Thwackey had a better chance."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Both unwilling to concede, Perrin captured their defiant expressions with her camera. These photos turned out great too.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After parting ways with the photographer, Summer and Marnie sat on the bench again. The sun now cast a golden glow on the river.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Today was really fun. Thanks for accompanying me, Summer. It would've been great to finish our battle~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Marnie suddenly asked, "Where's the Yell Team now?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"When did you notice?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"From the start. Summer, you're a forest ranger. You wouldn't just wander Motostoke. The Yell Team must have brought you here. I know what they're like~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Expectation isn't pressure but motivation. Whether it's you or everyone in Spikemuth, their support warms my heart."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Marnie touched her cheek, smiling more naturally than before.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"This is the only smile I can manage now, but I'll learn to smile genuinely. Then I can respond sincerely to everyone's encouragement," her blue eyes sparkled with hope.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Understanding how the Yell Team felt, Summer nodded, smiling back, "I'll look forward to that."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
