Both are in the southwest! A bold hypothesis formed in Summer's mind. Eleph's husband Simon must have accidentally entered the Gate to the Spirit World, a special portal that only opens at certain times, hence the lack of any trace of him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Leader Eleph, can you tell me when your husband went missing?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Why is this young traveler asking such questions? But from his demeanor, he might have discovered something. Could there be a clue about Simon?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"October 31st, which is four days from now. I'll never forget that date. Do you know something? Please, tell me!" Eleph pleaded. She didn't want to miss any leads.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hearing Eleph's answer, Summer asked in his mind, when does the Gate to the Spirit World in Glimwood Tangle open?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
[October 31st, at dusk, four days from now.]\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
As I suspected, my guess is likely correct, but the Spirit World is a dangerous place. Should I really tell her?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"You know something. Please, I beg you, tell me! I'll do anything you ask," Eleph pleaded humbly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"But you still have Opal."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Opal..." Thinking of her daughter, Eleph's tone became hesitant. He must be reluctant to tell me because it's dangerous.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Bang! The wooden door was pushed open forcefully, and Opal stood outside, shouting, "Please, big brother, tell Mom. It's about Dad, isn't it?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Opal, eavesdropping is not a good habit." Summer sighed, covering his forehead. "Fine, it's the Spirit World. I suspect Opal's father is lost in the Spirit World."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The Spirit World... But isn't that a world only for the dead?" Eleph clearly knew about the Spirit World.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No, to be honest, I came to Glimwood Tangle to find the Gate to the Spirit World, a magical door connecting this world to the Spirit World," Summer said, giving himself a reason for being in Glimwood Tangle.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Because it connects two worlds, it's possible for a living person to get lost in the Spirit World. His disappearance time matches the opening time of the gate, which is why I have this suspicion."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Listen, the Spirit World is a very dangerous place. Ghost-type Pok\u233?mon there are almost always a threat to humans. That's why I hesitated to tell you."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"If what you say is true, then Simon must be alive. That's wonderful." Eleph spoke with a quiver in her voice.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Why?" Summer was puzzled.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Because mere Ghost-type Pok\u233?mon wouldn't be able to harm my husband. I know his strength very well." Eleph's expression was firm. "So tell me where the Gate to the Spirit World is. I'm not a weak, cowardly wife!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"And I'm not a weak, cowardly daughter!" Opal added.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Alright. Based on my guess, the Gate to the Spirit World is in the southwest part of Glimwood Tangle."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ah, no wonder you wanted to come to Stow-on-Side. It's the center of Glimwood Tangle. But won't we get lost on the way there?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Cough... Anyway, going to the Spirit World is very dangerous. We must be prepared, like having a Pok\u233?mon such as a Dusknoir." Summer said this because Dusknoir can freely travel between this world and the Spirit World.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dusknoir? I understand. I'll make the preparations."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After learning about her husband, Eleph was full of energy. She immediately picked up the phone and started making arrangements.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The next morning, an elderly man in a suit arrived at Glimwood Tangle, bringing a Pok\u233? Ball that contained a Dusknoir.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Miss, you should let go of your obsession. But why do you need this Pok\u233?mon? It can't bring back the souls of the dead," the old man advised.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The dead? No, I'm bringing back the living!" Eleph tossed the Pok\u233? Ball into the air, and a fearsome Pok\u233?mon with a gray-black body and a single red eye appeared.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
According to Summer, the Spirit World is vast, and each gate leads to different areas. Dusknoir can sense information from the corresponding area in the Spirit World.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Dusknoir, is there a living person in the nearby Spirit World?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hearing such a question, Dusknoir couldn't help but laugh. This forest has few people, and the Spirit World gate only opens once a year. What are the odds? Then its expression froze because it received a signal from the Spirit World.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Finally, a Dusknoir is here! Quickly send this living person back. He's been in the Spirit World for almost two years!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
(End of Chapter)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
