{\qc
64: Chapter 64: The Spirit World Gatekeeper\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It was said that Eternatus, an ancient entity infused with a powerful curse, started acting after absorbing the souls of Yamask. But just how many souls had this gigantic Eternatus consumed to reach this size?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Roar!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dusknoir let out a growl, signaling the massive Eternatus not to attack. The three before them were living beings and needed to be returned to their original world.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I. Don't. Care!" the colossal Eternatus hissed, "Howard. Must. Die!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The enormous arm of Eternatus, radiating a chilling aura, smashed down towards the ground.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dusknoir realized why the gatekeeper had gone berserk\u8212?it was influenced by memories from its previous life. Among these three people was a descendant of someone it deeply resented.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I won't let you harm our benefactor! Alcremie, use that move!" Simon shouted, tossing his Pok\u233? Ball into the air. Seven Alcremie of different decorations and colors appeared before him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
