"A child, at this hour?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The child, hearing Summer's murmurs, turned around in a panic. Its mask was as green as grass, gleaming brightly in the night.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"A glowing mask, could it be...?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
By moonlight, the child saw Summer's face, realizing he wasn't from Kitakami. Summer radiated a warm, friendly aura, a feeling the child hadn't experienced in a long time.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Boni~?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Sure enough, not a human but a Pok\u233?mon," Summer whispered. The Pok\u233?mon in front of him was probably the legendary ogre. Scary? No, pitiful. Watching the mask stall alone at night was too sad.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The people of Kitakami feared the ogre, and now it seemed the ogre feared them too. Why else would it come to the festival at this hour?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Festival of Masks. The ogre wore a mask like a human child. Kitakami villagers feared the ogre, so they wore masks at the festival. It made sense\u8212?the ogre could only approach people during this time, using its mask to blend in.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Recalling the ogre's residence, Summer thought about how dark and narrow it was, unworthy of being called a home. Did the ogre spend the rest of the year alone there?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The ogre wasn't indifferent to people's rejection; it was a lonely Pok\u233?mon, enjoying brief happiness once a year.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Was the Pok\u233?mon companion really as brave as the legend said? Should they believe the Kitakami villagers' tales without knowing the truth?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Hu." Summer exhaled deeply and then said to his partner, "Rilla, let's play some music to recall beautiful memories."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Rilla!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rilla placed its drum on the ground. It could feel Summer's emotions and decided to play joyful music to forget the troubles.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Boom~~~"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Pon?!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The sudden drum sound startled the ogre, making it jump back. Its small feet slipped, and the mask fell to the ground with a thud.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Rilla continued playing. The lively drumbeats stirred precious memories in the ogre's heart, like a spring gushing forth.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
By moonlight, Summer saw the true face behind the ogre's mask. It had an orange face like a tangerine, yellow eyes with star-shaped pupils, and small fangs that added a playful touch.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Scary? No, very cute. It was hard to associate it with the word "ogre."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
