Fezandipiti knew the fewest moves among the three, clearly not fond of battling.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That's all for now. First, apologize to Ogerpon sincerely," Summer said seriously.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The Loyal Three exchanged looks, then lowered their heads and made apologetic sounds. They had been wrong, regardless of the reasons, and had caused Ogerpon irreparable harm, an unchangeable fact.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Caw!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ogerpon puffed up its chest in response, forgiving them. It was generous and big-hearted.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Remember, Ogerpon, anyone can make mistakes. If they sincerely apologize, forgive them," the man's words echoed in Ogerpon's mind. Now it had done so.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Summer reached out to comfort the softly crying Ogerpon. He made a silent vow that if he ever met the Loyal Three's former master, he would make them pay.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
