115: Chapter 115: The Blood Moon's Past\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Summer walked through the Eternal Forest, surrounded by the web-spinning String Balls hanging from the trees, the Caterpie poking its head out of the soil, and the Vulpix leaving a crimson shadow as it moved through the woods.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
His impression of this forest was singular: an untouched primeval forest.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Since this forest was a replica of Kitakami's primeval forest, the Eternal Forest of Kitakami should be similar.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Summer wondered why the residents of Meadow Town, despite their small number, hadn't ventured into such a resource-rich forest. It seemed strange unless...\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This forest harbored extremely dangerous entities, much like Oni Mountain, where the legend of the ogres made villagers avoid the back mountains where ogres lived.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ogerpon, stay alert. This forest might have dangerous creatures," Summer said, observing his surroundings closely. It was strange; the area was becoming increasingly quiet, and the number of Pok\u233?mon was decreasing.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Ogerpon mimicked Summer's actions, placing its hand on its forehead to look around, and indeed, it sensed a powerful presence.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Gao!" it alerted Summer.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Oh, I feel it too. That sound of footsteps must belong to a big Pok\u233?mon," Summer inhaled deeply. "I hope it's a gentle giant\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Thud! Thud! Thud! The ground trembled more violently. Ogerpon pressed close to Summer, gripping its Thorn Whip tightly, and stared intently in the direction of the footsteps.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"What exactly is this mist\u8230?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Dense mist rose around them. Could it be a Pok\u233?mon that controls mist? And its size\u8230? Summer couldn't pinpoint it from memory.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
