The black and white space was filled with decay and coldness, with Ghost Pok\u233?mon drifting around, terrifying Jorio. He ran frantically, trying to escape this nightmarish world.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Time in the Spirit Realm differed from reality, and no one knew how long Jorio ran. After fainting, a mysterious entity threw him out of the Spirit Realm, back into the reality he longed for.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ah, don't kill me... Ah, ghosts, all ghosts... Oleana, save me!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Jorio woke up struggling and shouting, still immersed in the fear of the Spirit Realm.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hearing "Oleana," Summer realized this guy was sent by her. Oleana, Rose's confidant, usually acted on his behalf, though sometimes she acted on her own for his sake.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Who are you, and why are you here?" Summer asked coldly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Eek, my name is Jorio, I... Who are you! Why did you tie me up! This is a crime, you know!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Jorio, recognizing Summer as a person, quickly reverted to his usual attitude.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Summer couldn't tell if Jorio was weak-willed or determined, but he clearly didn't remember shouting Oleana's name in his dazed state.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So, Jorio's presence in Sunset Forest was likely due to Oleana's initiative.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Mr. Jorio, may I ask what the device in your backpack is for?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It's none of your business! Let me go!" Jorio shouted hysterically.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Summer replied calmly, "Looks like I'll need to ask your beloved Oleana. Ah, you mentioned something about seeing each other in the next life and loving only her..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ugh... Ah...!" Jorio's pale face turned red, gasping heavily. His current torment was ten times worse than what he endured in the Spirit Realm.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If Oleana knew he acted without permission, she'd be disappointed. If it implicated her, he'd regret it deeply. And she mustn't know he liked her!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"It has nothing to do with her! It was all me! Don't involve her!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"No, I believe Oleana is from Macro Cosmos..."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I'm here to detect energy fluctuations!" Jorio shouted, interrupting Summer with wide eyes.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"We detected strange energy fluctuations in this forest earlier, so I decided to investigate. It was all my initiative; she had nothing to do with it!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Energy fluctuations? Summer recalled the green light from the Meadow Plate spreading in Sunset Forest. Could that be it?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
So, Macro Cosmos was monitoring energy fluctuations across Galar, likely searching for Wishing Stars, crucial for awakening Eternatus.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
My guess was right\u8212?Rose is pursuing that plan.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But this guy hasn't actually broken any laws, so I can't detain him. Seeking explanations from Macro Cosmos would only draw Rose's attention.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
It's better to leave him as an Oleana-obsessed fool, but I'll make sure he never dares to step into Sunset Forest again.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"In light of your honesty, I can let you go," Summer said with a gentle smile.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This only made Jorio more frightened, thinking Summer might kill him to silence him.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Listen, you can't come back to this forest, or I'll post your statements online. Most importantly, you wouldn't want your dear Oleana to know, right?" Summer patted Jorio's hard shoulder.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"A loyal subordinate or a foolish one, which impression do you want to leave on her?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"The answer is obvious, isn't it?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"I agree! I'll pretend I was never here!" The vines binding Jorio loosened suddenly, and he nearly collapsed, never wanting to return to this forest.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Good choice. Now get lost."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Jorio picked up his backpack and fled Sunset Forest, but Summer felt no relief, as his suspicions were confirmed.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Another issue remained: how many Ghost Pok\u233?mon escaped from the Spirit Realm Gate? Summer still had to verify their safety and count, giving him a headache.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Phew, Nuzleaf, did you remember his face?"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yaha!" Nuzleaf nodded.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Good, blacklist him and anyone in the same uniform. Please inform everyone."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yaha!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
After instructing Nuzleaf, Summer turned to Rillaboom and the admiring Ogerpon.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Now we have work to do. Let's find the additional Ghost Pok\u233?mon."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Rilla," Rillaboom nodded silently.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Ogerpon!" Ogerpon was excited, seeing a rare side of Summer, like when it wore its Hearthflame Mask.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Though a massive task, Pok\u233?mon assistance made it manageable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Hatterene had the most success, quickly locating Ghost Pok\u233?mon hidden in the forest with its sensing ability. It found a group of Sinistea capable of hosting a tea party.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Other Ghost Pok\u233?mon were found by Phantump and its search team, including three Misdreavus, five Pumpkaboo, and one Gourgeist.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Misdreavus posed little threat, only scaring people to collect terror energy without harming anyone. So, Summer kept the three Misdreavus.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Pumpkaboo and Gourgeist, being Grass-type, easily made a forest pact with Summer.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
They wouldn't lure humans into the Spirit Realm, and Summer provided them a good home in Sunset Forest.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If not absorbing human energy, they'd spend most time in the soil, absorbing nutrients. Summer placed them in the serene Dream Forest, even planting an Aspear Berry tree nearby.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With this, all escaped Ghost Pok\u233?mon were dealt with, and Sunset Forest had a few new residents.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
(End of Chapter)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} 
