The calamity of the tablet eroded thoughts with its invisible, eerie words, causing people to lose the will to fight.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The calamity of the magatama tormented the mind with jealousy, causing irrationality.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The calamity of the cauldron tormented the mind with fear, causing loss of judgment.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The calamity of the sword on Glaseado Mountain induced a bone-chilling fear of death, causing people to give up resistance.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Therefore, one must maintain a firm will and not show any slackness when fighting the calamities.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Summer was grateful that he had strengthened his mental resistance earlier; otherwise, he would have doubted his ability to face the calamity of the sword directly.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The last ability was a combination of the previous two, which Yagen named "Great Calamity." In simple terms, the raging blizzard would become the carrier of the calamity of the sword's fear, doubling the torment on both mind and body.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Finally, my conjecture: they all possess a sinister and evil power, likely with something in common," Yagen said, looking at Summer. "You, coming from the future, might know that this power is countered by Lucario, who can also suppress Cresselia and Wyrdeer."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Yes, probably Dark-type energy, a type of energy comparable to elemental energy. Yagen, I suggest you use Lucario as the main attacker," Summer said.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Based on Yagen's description, the calamity of the sword should be an Ice and Dark-type Pok\u233?mon, making Lucario a natural counter, especially with Yagen's Aura powers aiding it.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
