Halfway through her sentence, Marnie's embarrassment surged. She suddenly stood up, holding Morpeko tightly, and said hurriedly, "It's getting late. I should go now."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"That reminds me. You're right," Summer nodded silently. He felt that if Marnie stayed any longer, Piers would soon come barging in.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Summer, sweet dreams. I had a great time today."\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
With that, Marnie quickly left the cabin. This embarrassing thing is something I especially don't want you to know.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
(End of the chapter)\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} 
