Meanwhile, the Pok\u233?mon egg from the Ranger Exam had yet to hatch. Given that it was a pseudo-legendary, this wasn't surprising. These eggs took much longer to incubate compared to Bug- or Grass-type Pok\u233?mon eggs, which would have hatched by now.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For the past few days, Ogerpon had been glued to the egg, refusing to leave its side even for a moment. Normally energetic and playful, she was now unusually calm and focused\u8212?a clear sign of just how much she was looking forward to this new life.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Inside the wooden cabin, Summer made his final preparations for the Time Distortion.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
