254: Chapter 254: Kubfu\u8217?s First Day in Sunset Forest\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar}\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Having achieved his goal, Summer returned to the familiar embrace of Sunset Forest, bringing with him an unexpected new companion\u8212?Kubfu.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Marnie, meanwhile, had decided to stay behind on the Isle of Armor for a while longer, ensuring she was fully prepared for her upcoming battle against Raihan. The Gym Challenge was nearing its final stretch, with only a handful of challengers remaining. Even fewer would make it past the final test.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Summer agreed with her decision completely. Mustard himself had offered to train her, and with that kind of guidance, Marnie's strength would undoubtedly soar to new heights.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\u8212?---\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Outside his wooden cabin, Summer released Kubfu from its Pok\u233? Ball.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
The little bear burst into motion the second it landed, running in excited circles around him, eyes shining with enthusiasm.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
This place was perfect for training!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Kubfu had assumed Sunset Forest would be similar to the Focused Forest back on the Isle of Armor, but after actually experiencing it firsthand, it realized that this place was overflowing with pure, concentrated life energy.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
For a Pok\u233?mon like Kubfu, this was invaluable.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Its lower abdomen housed a special organ called the Tanden, which generated Fighting-type energy. The more refined its breathing technique, the faster and stronger this energy would flow.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And breathing in life energy from the air? That was the best kind of training it could possibly get!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Planting its feet firmly on the ground, Kubfu assumed a deep horse stance and focused on regulating its breathing, allowing its Tanden to absorb the rich, potent energy of Sunset Forest.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
A satisfied smile crept onto its face.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\u8212?---\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Nearby, Corviknight, who had just finished its morning flight, watched the scene in shock.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
First, it had been Jangmo-o\u8212?the baby Dragon who had been training non-stop since day one.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
And now, this little bear had arrived and was already throwing itself into training the moment it stepped into the forest?!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Corviknight felt a sudden sense of crisis.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
If these young ones kept working this hard\u8230? would it lose its reputation as the strongest?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No\u8212?unacceptable!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Corviknight had always been the one boasting about its intense training regimen.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
How could it let the rookies steal its thunder?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No more slacking off!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
No more card games!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Corviknight flapped its wings fiercely, launching itself into the sky.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
"Caw! (Summer, I'm heading out to train!)"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Summer watched it soar away, feeling mildly amused.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Had Corviknight just gotten jealous of Kubfu's enthusiasm?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
Honestly, that wouldn't be surprising. Ever since unlocking its "Windborn" potential, Corviknight had slacked off on training quite a bit. These days, it spent most of its time lounging in the treetops, sometimes even playing card games for hours.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
But now that it had new competition?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
